  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This is a flat scarf worked in fern lace on 4 mm needles with DK yarn, finishing at 20 cm wide and 175 cm long after blocking. The pattern works an eight-row repeat of branching "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "yarn-over"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "yarn-overs"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " and "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "k2tog"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "K2tog"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " / "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "ssk"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "SSK"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " decreases. The central decrease column divides each repeat; yarn-overs walk outward then converge inward to trace the branching frond shape."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Flat construction suits this lace because the right-side pattern rows determine the stitch placement. All wrong-side rows are purled, which simplifies the work. The chart should be read alongside the written instructions, as the eight-row repeat is easier to track visually than from text alone. The scarf uses about 175 g (395 m / 432 yards) of DK yarn."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "suppliesCard",
        "attrs": {
          "heading": "Materials",
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "DK-weight wool or wool-blend yarn",
              "qty": "175 g (approx. 395 m / 432 yards)",
              "substitutions": "A smooth, non-splitting yarn makes the fern motif easier to read."
            },
            {
              "name": "4 mm needles (UK 8 / US 6)",
              "qty": "1 pair or 1 circular",
              "substitutions": ""
            },
            {
              "name": "Blocking mat and rust-proof pins",
              "qty": "required",
              "substitutions": ""
            },
            {
              "name": "Tapestry or darning needle",
              "qty": "1",
              "substitutions": ""
            },
            {
              "name": "Scissors",
              "qty": "1 pair",
              "substitutions": ""
            },
            {
              "name": "Measuring tape",
              "qty": "1",
              "substitutions": ""
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Gauge"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "22 sts x 30 rows = 10 x 10 cm in stocking stitch on 4 mm needles. Fern lace opens to approximately 20 sts per 10 cm after blocking. Swatch in pattern and measure after blocking before starting the full scarf."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Stitches used"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "K (knit), P (purl), YO (yarn over), K2tog, SSK. On RS rows, work the written pattern. On WS rows, purl to end."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pattern"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Cast on"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Cast on 46 stitches using the long-tail cast-on: 2 selvedge stitches each side and 42 pattern stitches (a multiple of 11 with 9 remaining handled in the selvedge columns). Note: the pattern uses 2 repeats of 11 stitches = 22 stitches, plus 2 plain selvedge columns of 11 stitches each, plus 2 selvedge edge stitches = 46 total. Tail length: (12.6 x 46) / 10 + 15 = about 73 cm."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Stitch count check-in: 46 stitches after the cast-on."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Body"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Row 1 (RS): K2 (selvedge), *K1, YO, K2, K2tog, K1, SSK, K2, YO, K1; repeat from * to last 2 sts, K2 (selvedge). (46 sts)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Row 2 and all WS rows: P to end. (46 sts)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Row 3 (RS): K2, *K2, YO, K1, K2tog, K1, SSK, K1, YO, K2; repeat from * to last 2 sts, K2. (46 sts)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Row 5 (RS): K2, *K3, YO, K2tog, K1, SSK, YO, K3; repeat from * to last 2 sts, K2. (46 sts)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Row 7 (RS): K2, *K4, K2tog, YO, SSK, K4; repeat from * to last 2 sts, K2. Note: this row has K2tog followed immediately by SSK with a single YO between them (the tip of the frond). (46 sts)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Repeat the 8-row pattern until the scarf measures 175 cm from the cast-on edge, blocked. At the halfway mark (about 87 cm), count: still 46 stitches."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Cast off"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Cast off after a Row 2 (WS) or Row 8 using the standard method. Work loosely."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Common faults"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Fern motif misaligned. The YOs walk outward across Rows 1-5 and converge again in Row 7. If the positions shift, the frond silhouette breaks up. Use the chart to track where each YO should land relative to the central K2tog/SSK pair."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Stitch count changing. Each RS row has exactly 2 YOs and 2 decreases per repeat. Count before and after every RS row."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pattern unclear before blocking. The fern shape reads vaguely off the needles and becomes distinct only after blocking. Thread a lifeline every 80 rows before blocking a section to confirm the pattern is working as intended."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Finishing"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Weave in ends. Wet "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "blocking"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "blocking"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " is essential: soak, press out moisture, and pin flat. The fern fronds will open and become clearly defined after blocking."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Care"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Handwash in cool water and lay flat to dry."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What to try next"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The leaf lace scarf uses a similar branching repeat with more stitch variation. The lace stole works a comparable pattern at fingering weight for a finer, larger piece."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}